<script lang="ts">
	import { examples } from '../../utils/examples'

	const drawer = signal(false)
	const drafts = signal(false)
	const query = signal('')
	const pages = [
		{ title: 'UIDrawer', url: '#drawer' },
		{ title: 'UITooltip', url: '#tooltip' },
		{ title: 'UICommandPalette', url: '#command-palette' },
	]
	const results = computed(() => pages.filter((page) => page.title.toLowerCase().includes(query.value.trim().toLowerCase())))
</script>

<template>
	<DocsPage
		locale="en"
		title="Overlays"
		description="Drawer, Tooltip and CommandPalette, on top of native dialog and popover."
	>
		<p>
			For a dialog with a result, use
			<MeekoLink to="/modals">Modal</MeekoLink>
			; for a menu or a lightweight dialog,
			<MeekoLink to="/popover">Popover</MeekoLink>
			. They all use the top layer of the browser, and leave with a View Transition where it exists.
		</p>
		<h2 id="drawer">UIDrawer</h2>
		<p>
			A side panel. It is a modal
			<code>dialog</code>
			with
			<code>command</code>
			,
			<code>commandfor</code>
			and
			<code>closedby</code>
			: it opens, closes and returns the focus without JavaScript in the browsers that support them; elsewhere, on hydration. Following a link inside closes it at once, because the navigation already is the transition.
		</p>
		<DocsPreview>
			<UIDrawer
				title="Filters"
				triggerLabel="Open filters"
				side="end"
				model="drawer"
			>
				<UICheckbox
					label="Include drafts"
					model="drafts"
				/>
				<snippet name="footer">
					<UIButton on:click="() => (drawer.value = false)">Apply</UIButton>
				</snippet>
			</UIDrawer>
		</DocsPreview>
		<DocsCode bind:code="examples.drawer" />
		<DocsApi
			caption="UIDrawer props"
			bind:rows="[
				{ name: 'title', type: 'string', description: 'Required. Name of the dialog.' },
				{ name: 'model', type: 'Signal<boolean>', default: 'false', description: 'Open state, two-way.' },
				{ name: 'side', type: 'start | end', default: 'start', description: 'The side it enters from.' },
				{ name: 'triggerLabel / closeLabel', type: 'string', description: 'Text of the trigger and accessible name of the close button.' },
				{ name: 'closedBy', type: 'any | closerequest | none', default: 'any', description: 'What closes it besides its button: the backdrop and Esc, only Esc or nothing.' },
				{ name: 'closeOnNavigate', type: 'boolean', default: 'true', description: 'It closes when following a link.' },
				{ name: 'id / class', type: 'string', description: 'Identity and classes.' },
			]"
		/>
		<p>
			It accepts the
			<code>default</code>
			,
			<code>footer</code>
			and
			<code>trigger(id)</code>
			snippets, and the
			<code>close</code>
			event.
		</p>
		<h2 id="tooltip">UITooltip</h2>
		<p>
			A
			<MeekoLink to="/popover">UIPopover</MeekoLink>
			with
			<code>mode="hint"</code>
			and the look of a tooltip: it opens with the pointer or the focus, never takes the focus, and the trigger references it with
			<code>aria-describedby</code>
			. Write complementary information in it.
		</p>
		<DocsPreview>
			<UITooltip text="It is published when saved">
				<snippet name="trigger">When is it published?</snippet>
			</UITooltip>
		</DocsPreview>
		<DocsCode bind:code="examples.tooltip" />
		<DocsApi
			caption="UITooltip props"
			bind:rows="[
				{ name: 'text', type: 'string', description: 'The text; for anything else, the default snippet.' },
				{ name: 'placement', type: 'PopoverPlacement', default: 'top', description: 'Side and alignment.' },
				{ name: 'offset', type: 'number', default: '6', description: 'Separation in pixels.' },
				{ name: 'delay / closeDelay', type: 'number', default: '300 / 150', description: 'Milliseconds before opening and closing.' },
				{ name: 'class / triggerClass / triggerId', type: 'string', description: 'Classes of the content and the trigger, and id of the trigger.' },
			]"
		/>
		<p>
			It accepts the
			<code>default</code>
			,
			<code>trigger</code>
			and
			<code>anchor(trigger)</code>
			snippets, for a trigger of your own.
		</p>
		<h2 id="command-palette">UICommandPalette</h2>
		<p>
			It does not search: read
			<code>query</code>
			in your code, search wherever you want (Pagefind, a server or a local list) and pass it
			<code>results</code>
			and
			<code>status</code>
			. It opens with its button or with
			<code>Ctrl</code>
			and
			<code>K</code>
			, and the arrows walk the results without taking the focus out of the field.
		</p>
		<DocsPreview>
			<UICommandPalette
				label="Search this page"
				hrefBy="url"
				labelBy="title"
				model:query="query"
				bind:results="results.value"
				bind:status="results.value.length ? 'ready' : 'empty'"
			/>
		</DocsPreview>
		<DocsCode bind:code="examples.commandPalette" />
		<DocsApi
			caption="UICommandPalette props"
			bind:rows="[
				{ name: 'results', type: 'readonly T[]', description: 'Required. What shows.' },
				{ name: 'status', type: 'idle | loading | ready | empty | unavailable', default: 'ready', description: 'What the status region announces.' },
				{ name: 'model / model:query / model:active', type: 'Signal', description: 'Open state, searched text and active result.' },
				{ name: 'labelBy / hrefBy / childrenBy', type: 'key or function', description: 'Label, target and nested results.' },
				{ name: 'label / inputLabel / placeholder / closeLabel', type: 'string', description: 'Texts. The default values follow the language of the document.' },
				{ name: 'trigger / shortcut', type: 'boolean', default: 'true', description: 'Paints its button and listens to the shortcut.' },
				{ name: 'inputId / inputName / class / triggerClass', type: 'string', description: 'Identity of the field and classes.' },
			]"
		/>
		<p>
			It accepts the
			<code>item(item, state)</code>
			,
			<code>trigger(modifier)</code>
			and
			<code>status(status, query)</code>
			snippets, and the
			<code>open</code>
			,
			<code>close</code>
			and
			<code>choose</code>
			events. The types
			<code>UIDrawerProps</code>
			,
			<code>UITooltipProps</code>
			and
			<code>UICommandPaletteProps</code>
			are exported from
			<code>@meekojs/ui/runtime</code>
			.
		</p>
	</DocsPage>
</template>
